          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "By [L1], canonical energy concentration permits construction of a sequence $\\widehat\\delta_n\\downarrow0$ such that the shell has positive measure eventually and its uniform conditional law, the exact-$N$ canonical law, and the matching grand law have the same local-tame limit $P^\\ast$; [L3] independently gives the stated canonical local convergence. Set $\\delta_n=E_0\\widehat\\delta_n$; therefore the physical shell widths shrink in joules per reference volume and expectations converge for each stated bounded-region observable of at-most-linear count growth.",
          "step": "2.1",
